simultaneously, meaning C must occupy 1 person across all 6 days while A, B, and D fit into the remaining 3.\n\nTrying sequences: B first (days 1-3) then A leaves no room since only 1 free slot remains, and A-then-B pushes D to day 7, over budget. Testing B days 1-3 with A days 4-6 instead to see if that fits.\n\nCombining A (3 people) with either D (2) or B (2) always hits 6 people alongside C's 1 person, exceeding capacity — so A can never overlap with B or D. This means A must occupy a standalone window, while B must precede D in the sequence.\n\nTesting orderings: A-B-D and B-D-A both total 7 days, exceeding the 6-day limit. B-A-D also forces B to finish before D starts, but the total still overshoots 6 days regardless of arrangement, so I need to reconsider whether any partial overlap between segments could still satisfy the people constraint.\n\nSince B must precede D and they can't overlap, B(3)+D(2)=5 sequential days, leaving only 1 day for A which needs 2 days — that doesn't work no matter where A is placed among the remaining slots.\n\nI check whether A could squeeze into B's idle slot, but A needs all 3 non-C people free, and B only frees up 1. So this schedule genuinely doesn't fit — it needs at least 7 days total, not 6.\n\nPlacing A before or after B-then-D still totals 2+3+2=7 days, exceeding the 6-day limit no matter the order. There's no way to fit all three tasks into 6 days with these constraints.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4604,"cache_read_input_tokens":5701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4604},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6375fb08-34c6-4f2b-bae7-8f791db4cb5b","uuid":"ee44698e-b7ff-4d47-8b63-45ebf05065f9"}
